<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-constantinople-1204"><span class="enc-name">Sack of Constantinople (1204)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1204</span><span class="enc-snip">The sack of Constantinople in 1204 was the capture and plunder of the Byzantine capital by the army of the Fourth Crusade, supported by Venice.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-caizhou"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Caizhou</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1233–1234</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Caizhou in 1233 and 1234 was the final campaign against the Jurchen Jin dynasty in China.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-cordoba"><span class="enc-name">Fall of Córdoba</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1236</span><span class="enc-snip">The fall of Córdoba was the capture of the city by Ferdinand III of Castile in 1236.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mali-conquest-of-koumbi-saleh"><span class="enc-name">Mali conquest of Koumbi Saleh</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1240</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mali conquest of Koumbi Saleh in 1240 was the capture of the former capital of the Ghana Empire by the forces of Sundiata Keita.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-seville"><span class="enc-name">Fall of Seville</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1248</span><span class="enc-snip">The fall of Seville was the capture of the city by Ferdinand III of Castile in 1248 after a long siege.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-alamut"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-alamut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Alamut</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1256</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Alamut was the capture of the mountain